Errors and warnings whose text lacks the newline are still lines of
their own (#4689).

msgline prints two errors without a newline from its setup, which runs
in the main thread of rtapi_app, and an error and a warning without a
newline from its function, whose messages rtapi_app queues and prints
from another thread. Each must be a line of its own in the output. An
info message printed in two parts must stay one line: the levels other
than errors and warnings may build a line from several messages.
